window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-c87fd8be013036dc"]={"zh":"<p><a id=\"production-systems\"></a></p> <h1 id=\"_1\">生产环境系统</h1> <blockquote> <p>如需查看完整文档索引，请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。将 <code>.md</code> 附加到页面 URL 后，可查看该页面的 Markdown 版本。</p> </blockquote> <p>理解、重构并审阅真实代码库。</p> <p>当 Codex 处理的代码库已有历史记录、测试、负责人和生产环境约束时，可以参考本集合中的用例。Codex 特别擅长在复杂代码库中定位和理解代码，包括包含大量服务和依赖项的大型单体仓库。如果你正在处理生产系统，可以从这些用例了解 Codex 能如何提供帮助。</p> <p><a id=\"start-with-a-codebase-tour\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_2\">先熟悉代码库</h2> <p>让 Codex 帮你熟悉复杂代码库；如果你刚开始接手一个生产软件代码库，这尤其有用。</p> <ul> <li><a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/use-cases/codebase-onboarding\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">理解大型代码库（本地尚未收录）</a>：让 Codex 梳理陌生代码库，解释不同模块和数据流，并指出……</li> </ul> <p><a id=\"modernize-the-codebase\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_3\">现代化改造代码库</h2> <p>让 Codex 规划技术栈迁移，在适用时将 API 集成升级到最新模型，并通过重构提高代码库的可读性和可维护性。</p> <ul> <li><a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/use-cases/api-integration-migrations\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">升级 API 集成（本地尚未收录）</a>：让 Codex 将现有 OpenAI API 集成更新为当前推荐的模型……</li> <li><a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/use-cases/refactor-your-codebase\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">重构代码库（本地尚未收录）</a>：让 Codex 删除无用代码、理清大型文件、合并重复逻辑，并……</li> <li><a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/use-cases/code-migrations\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">执行代码迁移（本地尚未收录）</a>：让 Codex 梳理旧系统迁移到新技术栈的方式，分阶段实施并验证……</li> </ul> <p><a id=\"codify-repeatable-work\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_4\">将可重复工作流程整理成规范</h2> <p>让 Codex 把代码库特有的工作流程或检查清单整理成 Skill，让所有代码库贡献者都能使用统一流程。</p> <ul> <li><a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/use-cases/reusable-codex-skills\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">将工作流程保存为 Skill（本地尚未收录）</a>：把有效的 Codex 对话、审查规则、测试命令、发布检查清单和设计……</li> </ul> <p><a id=\"keep-documentation-current\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_5\">保持文档最新</h2> <p>让 Codex 对照源代码变更和现有文档，只更新最必要的文档内容，并验证更新结果。</p> <ul> <li><a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/use-cases/update-documentation\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">保持文档更新（本地尚未收录）</a>：让 Codex 比较源代码变更、公开文档、发行说明和拉取请求背景，然后……</li> </ul> <p><a id=\"maintain-system-health\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_6\">维护系统健康</h2> <p>通过 Slack 让 Codex 自动处理功能请求和缺陷修复任务，并将其连接到告警工具、问题跟踪工具和日常缺陷排查流程。</p> <ul> <li><a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/use-cases/slack-coding-tasks\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">从 Slack 启动编码任务（本地尚未收录）</a>：在符合条件的工作区共享环境中，于 Slack 中提及 <code>@ChatGPT</code>，请求它处理代码库工作……</li> <li><a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/use-cases/automation-bug-triage\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">自动整理缺陷分诊（本地尚未收录）</a>：让 Codex 检查近期告警、问题、失败检查、日志和聊天报告，并调整……</li> </ul> <p><a id=\"avoid-the-review-bottleneck\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_7\">减少审查瓶颈</h2> <p>让 Codex 自动审查拉取请求并针对关键流程执行 QA，以便尽早发现问题并更有把握地交付。</p> <ul> <li><a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/use-cases/github-code-reviews\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">审查 GitHub 拉取请求（本地尚未收录）</a>：使用 GitHub 中的 Codex 代码审查，自动发现回归问题、缺失的测试以及……</li> <li><a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/use-cases/qa-your-app-with-computer-use\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">使用 Computer Use 测试应用（本地尚未收录）</a>：使用 Computer Use 操作关键流程、发现问题，并最终生成缺陷报告。</li> </ul>","en":"<h1 id=\"production-systems\">Production systems</h1> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <p>Navigate, refactor, and review real codebases.</p> <p>The use cases in this collection are useful when Codex is working in a repo that already has history, tests, owners, and production constraints. Codex is particularly good at navigating complex codebases, including sprawling monorepos with lots of different services and dependencies. If you're working on a production system, get familiar with these use cases to understand how Codex can help you.</p> <h2 id=\"start-with-a-codebase-tour\">Start with a codebase tour</h2> <p>Use Codex to get familiar with a complex codebase, which is especially useful when onboarding onto a repo for production software.</p> <ul> <li><a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/use-cases/codebase-onboarding\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Understand large codebases (not in this local snapshot)</a>: Use Codex to map unfamiliar codebases, explain different modules and data flow, and point...</li> </ul> <h2 id=\"modernize-the-codebase\">Modernize the codebase</h2> <p>Leverage Codex to plan tech stack migrations, upgrade your integration to the latest models if applicable, and refactor the codebase to improve readability and maintainability.</p> <ul> <li><a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/use-cases/api-integration-migrations\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Upgrade your API integration (not in this local snapshot)</a>: Use Codex to update your existing OpenAI API integration to the latest recommended models...</li> <li><a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/use-cases/refactor-your-codebase\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Refactor your codebase (not in this local snapshot)</a>: Use Codex to remove dead code, untangle large files, collapse duplicated logic, and...</li> <li><a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/use-cases/code-migrations\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Run code migrations (not in this local snapshot)</a>: Use Codex to map a legacy system to a new stack, land the move in milestones, and validate...</li> </ul> <h2 id=\"codify-repeatable-work\">Codify repeatable work</h2> <p>Ask Codex to turn repo-specific workflows or checklists into a skill, so that all repo contributors can benefit from a standardized process.</p> <ul> <li><a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/use-cases/reusable-codex-skills\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Save workflows as skills (not in this local snapshot)</a>: Turn a working Codex chat, review rules, test commands, release checklists, design...</li> </ul> <h2 id=\"keep-documentation-current\">Keep documentation current</h2> <p>Ask Codex to compare source changes with existing docs, update the smallest useful docs surface, and verify the changes.</p> <ul> <li><a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/use-cases/update-documentation\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Keep documentation up-to-date (not in this local snapshot)</a>: Use Codex to compare source code changes, public docs, release notes, and PR context, then...</li> </ul> <h2 id=\"maintain-system-health\">Maintain system health</h2> <p>Let Codex pick up feature requests and bug fixes automatically by using it from Slack and connecting it to your alerting, issue tracking, and daily bug sweeps.</p> <ul> <li><a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/use-cases/slack-coding-tasks\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Kick off coding tasks from Slack (not in this local snapshot)</a>: Mention <code>@ChatGPT</code> in Slack to request repository work in an eligible workspace-shared Codex...</li> <li><a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/use-cases/automation-bug-triage\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Automate bug triage (not in this local snapshot)</a>: Ask Codex to check recent alerts, issues, failed checks, logs, and chat reports, tune the...</li> </ul> <h2 id=\"avoid-the-review-bottleneck\">Avoid the review bottleneck</h2> <p>Use Codex to automatically review PRs and run focused QA passes on critical flows, so you can catch issues quickly and ship updates confidently.</p> <ul> <li><a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/use-cases/github-code-reviews\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Review GitHub pull requests (not in this local snapshot)</a>: Use Codex code review in GitHub to automatically surface regressions, missing tests, and...</li> <li><a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/use-cases/qa-your-app-with-computer-use\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">QA your app with Computer Use (not in this local snapshot)</a>: Use Computer Use to exercise key flows, catch issues, and finish with a bug report.</li> </ul>"};
